---
name: SGLang
description: "Any Hugging Face model SGLang supports, from its safetensors. Tensor-parallel across the GPUs the job gets on one node."
engine: sglang
kind: engine
requires: "An SGLang image that supports the model's architecture"
model_type: chat
api_model_name: my-model
port: 8000
health_path: /health
target_replicas: 1
max_job_failures: 2
tested:
  - hardware: "1× A100 80 GB"
    engine: "SGLang 0.5.21"
    date: 2026-10-03
    result: "Served openai/gpt-oss-20b with --tool-call-parser gpt-oss --reasoning-parser gpt-oss. Ready in 8.5 minutes. One request ran at about 125 tokens a second; 16 at once reached 430. Tool calls worked 3 times out of 3."
  - hardware: "1× GH200 96 GB"
    engine: "SGLang 0.5.21 (Arm)"
    date: 2026-10-03
    result: "Served openai/gpt-oss-20b with --tool-call-parser gpt-oss --reasoning-parser gpt-oss --attention-backend triton, since the Arm image lacks FlashAttention 3. Ready in 4 minutes. One request ran at about 245 tokens a second; 16 at once reached 985. Tool calls worked 3 times out of 3."
inputs:
  - name: model
    label: Hugging Face model
    type: text
    required: true
    help: The repo id, such as Qwen/Qwen3-32B, or a folder on the cluster that holds the weights.
  - name: context
    label: Context length
    type: number
    min: 1024
    default: 32768
    required: true
    unit: tokens
    help: The longest prompt and answer together. A longer context needs more GPU memory, and the model's own maximum may not fit.
  - name: extra
    label: More SGLang flags
    type: text
    help: "Anything else to pass to sglang.launch_server, written as on its command line, such as --tool-call-parser qwen25. With the official Arm image, add --attention-backend triton: it has no FlashAttention 3 kernels."
  - name: image
    label: Container image
    type: path
    default: "{{cluster.image.sglang}}"
    help: The image the server runs in. Leave it empty to run python3 with SGLang installed from the node's PATH, for example after the cluster's setup lines load it.
  - name: cache
    label: Weight cache
    type: path
    default: "{{cluster.cache}}"
    required: true
    help: Where the weights are kept between jobs. Use shared storage, so a restart on another node doesn't download them again.
---
#!/bin/bash -l
#SBATCH --gres=gpu:1
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=16
#SBATCH --mem=64G
# The cluster's setup lines run before strict mode, since site scripts often
# read unset variables.
{{cluster.setup}}
set -euo pipefail
export HF_HOME="{{cache}}"
# In the image when one is set, with the cluster's container command
# (OBLETH_CONTAINER_RUN, "apptainer exec --nv" when unset); else from the node's PATH.
IMAGE="{{image}}"
RUN=()
if [ -n "$IMAGE" ]; then
  read -r -a RUN <<< "${OBLETH_CONTAINER_RUN:-apptainer exec --nv}"
  RUN+=(--bind "$HF_HOME" "$IMAGE")
fi
exec ${RUN[@]+"${RUN[@]}"} python3 -m sglang.launch_server \
  --model-path {{model}} \
  --served-model-name {{api_model_name}} \
  --host 0.0.0.0 --port "$OBLETH_SERVING_PORT" \
  --tp "${SLURM_GPUS_ON_NODE:-1}" \
  --context-length {{context}} \
  {{extra}}
